From 5ac187bacafd34cf6cadd4b7690e2f3f6298c130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:08:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): placement carries kanban_create options through
 hermes-hub create-task --option [daveey]

hermes-hub 1.8.0 adds create-task --option KEY=JSON. When create-task --help lists it, default placement passes
skills, max_runtime_seconds, priority, model/provider, goal_mode, goal_max_turns, completion_contract,
requires and triage as fields, so model pins, goal mode, triage and PR contracts no longer pin a card local and
skills/runtime no longer ride as body text. An older client keeps the old rule and the body-text fallback.
The client probe is cached 10 min and runs only when a legacy-uncarried option is used.

Also: hermes kanban create --reasoning-effort (hermes-hub maps a plain create's reasoning_effort onto it), and
the BOM/FURB167 lint in scripts/run_tests_host_slots.py that kept scripts/check red on main.
